 "method": "Annual value = mean of the monthly not-seasonally-adjusted LAUS unemployment rates for the calendar year, rounded to one decimal. The keyless BLS v1 API does not return BLS's own annual averages, which BLS computes from annual-average unemployment and labor-force levels, so a year here can differ from the published annual average by about 0.1 point. Peers and boroughs are computed the same way.",
 "caveats": [
  "BLS published no October 2025 figure for LAUS areas (data collection lapsed during the October-November 2025 federal shutdown). The 2025 averages for New York, the peers and the boroughs are the mean of the 11 published months.",
  "Counts residents of the city by where they live, not where they work.",
  "LAUS city and county estimates are model-based and are revised each spring; the latest months are preliminary."
 ]
}
